<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<QuickAction xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!-- THIS NOTE LIVES IN A COMMENT INSIDE THE ROOT ELEMENT - a comment placed ABOVE
         <QuickAction> breaks `sf` deploy at source conversion. See
         NDA__c.Move_to_Received.quickAction-meta.xml for the full rationale behind finishing the
         acquisition side of this change (2026-08-27, completes a939e97) and for why there is no
         <description> element.

         THE HOP: Contract_Review__c acquisition sequence (Acquisition_PSA) is
         Draft -> Negotiation -> Signed -> Executed ('Executed' is terminal). This action serves
         Signed -> Executed, gated on Contract_Review_Record_Page by
         {!Record.Negotiation_Status__c} EQUAL 'Signed'.

         🔴 THE FIELD IS Negotiation_Status__c, NOT Stage__c - Stage__c on this object is DERIVED
         and unwritable, exactly as Contract_Review__c.Move_to_Negotiation's own comment records
         for the disposition side. A rule written against Stage__c here would look right and
         never fire.

         🔴 THIS IS THE HIGHEST-CONSEQUENCE RECORD-TYPE PIN IN THE WHOLE CHANGE.
         'Signed' is MID-SEQUENCE on Acquisition_PSA but TERMINAL on Disposition_PSA (the sell
         side's sequence was harmonised by the user on 2026-08-21 to
         Initial Draft -> Negotiation -> Signed). A stage-only rule would offer "Executed" on a
         COMPLETED sell-side PSA. And because Negotiation_Status__c is a RESTRICTED picklist whose
         record-type subset IS enforced by Apex DML (measured 2026-08-21,
         INVALID_OR_NULL_FOR_RESTRICTED_PICKLIST), and 'Executed' is NOT on the Disposition_PSA
         record type at all, the click would fail with an opaque platform error rather than the
         service's user-safe message.

         RECORD-TYPE POLARITY - the page criterion is
         {!Record.RecordType.DeveloperName} NE 'Disposition_PSA' (fails OPEN on Master, matching
         RecordStageAdvanceService's defaultTypeKey routing a Master row to the acquisition map).
         See NDA__c.Move_to_Received.quickAction-meta.xml for the full polarity argument. -->
    <actionSubtype>Action</actionSubtype>
    <label>Executed</label>
    <lightningWebComponent>advanceRecordStage</lightningWebComponent>
    <optionsCreateFeedItem>false</optionsCreateFeedItem>
    <type>LightningWebComponent</type>
</QuickAction>
